# Metrics

> Back to [README](../README.md)

Every metric `@@EXPORTER_NAME@@` can emit, grouped by collector. This file is kept
truthful by `make docs-check` (part of `make check`, see
[CONTRIBUTING.md](../CONTRIBUTING.md)'s Definition of Done): any metric or label
listed below that the code cannot actually produce fails the build. A metric the
code emits but this file doesn't document is only a warning: see
`internal/collector/docs_check_test.go`.

**Scope:** this file is shared by a `single`-target and a `multi`-target build
(a `--target-model multi-instance` build ships its own separate copy, with its
own reload and instance-label sections). A section or row below tagged
*(multi-target builds only)* or *(opt-in builds only)* is not a flag a
`single`-target binary could enable: the package backing it,
`internal/reload` or `internal/probe`, is not compiled into that binary at
all. If you scaffolded `single`, skip those sections entirely rather than
reading them as "off by default".

